  "__class__": "Meeting",
  "transcript": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": "00:11:56.190",
      "end": "00:12:05.910",
      "text": "Okay, I'm going to call the seventh meeting of council to order."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": "00:12:05.910",
      "end": "00:12:08.120",
      "text": "This is a special meeting of council."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": "00:12:08.120",
      "end": "00:12:10.900",
      "text": "So we do only have one agenda item."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": "00:12:10.900",
      "end": "00:12:17.820",
      "text": "I will just note off the top, I know there's a number of people in the audience today."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": "00:12:17.820",
      "end": "00:12:22.850",
      "text": "My understanding is that you're probably here for the SPPC meeting that starts at four,"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": "00:12:22.850",
      "end": "00:12:25.520",
      "text": "where there's an added agenda about a petition."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": "00:12:25.520",
      "end": "00:12:29.020",
      "text": "What we're doing today is a special council meeting to deal with one item, which is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": "00:12:29.020",
      "end": "00:12:35.270",
      "text": "timely matter related to a provincial transfer payment that we have to have done by a certain"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": "00:12:35.270",
      "end": "00:12:36.250",
      "text": "date."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": "00:12:36.250",
      "end": "00:12:39.560",
      "text": "So I just want you to know in case you don't see your item happen during the council meeting,"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": "00:12:39.560",
      "end": "00:12:42.490",
      "text": "it will be at the meeting that starts at four."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": "00:12:42.490",
      "end": "00:12:46.810",
      "text": "With that, I'm going to start with land acknowledgement."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": "00:12:46.810",
      "end": "00:12:49.680",
      "text": "We acknowledge that we are gathered today on the traditional lands of the Anishinaabak"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": "00:12:49.680",
      "end": "00:12:52.660",
      "text": "Haudenosaunee, Lene Peiwak, and Adawandran."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": "00:12:52.660",
      "end": "00:12:55.910",
      "text": "We honor and respect the history, languages, and culture of the diverse indigenous people"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": "00:12:55.910",
      "end": "00:12:58.030",
      "text": "who call this territory home."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": "00:12:58.030",
      "end": "00:13:00.980",
      "text": "We acknowledge all of the treaties that are specific to this area."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": "00:13:00.980",
      "end": "00:13:05.610",
      "text": "The two-row Wampum Belt Treaty of the Haudenosaunee Confederacy, Silver Covenant Chain, the Beaver"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": "00:13:05.610",
      "end": "00:13:11.930",
      "text": "Hunting Grounds of the Haudenosaunee, Nanfant Treaty of 1701, the McKee Treaty of 1790, the"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": "00:13:11.930",
      "end": "00:13:17.520",
      "text": "London Township Treaty of 1796, the Huron Track Treaty of 1827 with the Anishinaabak, and"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": "00:13:17.520",
      "end": "00:13:22.320",
      "text": "the Dish With One Spoon, Covenant Wampum of the Anishinaabak and Haudenosaunee."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": "00:13:22.320",
      "end": "00:13:26.020",
      "text": "The three indigenous nations that are neighbors to London are the Chippewas of the Thames First"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": "00:13:26.020",
      "end": "00:13:30.580",
      "text": "Nation, Oneida Nation of the Thames, and the Muncie Delaware Nation, who all continue to"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": "00:13:30.580",
      "end": "00:13:34.950",
      "text": "live as sovereign nations with individual and unique languages, cultures, and customs."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": "00:13:34.950",
      "end": "00:13:39.980",
      "text": "I'll also add that the City of London is committed to making every effort to provide alternate"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": "00:13:39.980",
      "end": "00:13:44.670",
      "text": "format, alternate formats, and communication supports for meetings upon request."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": "00:13:44.670",
      "end": "00:13:49.760",
      "text": "To make a request specific to this meeting, please contact Council Agenda at London.ca"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": "00:13:49.760",
      "end": "00:13:56.450",
      "text": "or 519-661-2489, extension 2425."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": "00:13:56.450",
      "end": "00:13:59.120",
      "text": "I will start with disclosures of pecuniary interest."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": "00:13:59.120",
      "end": "00:14:10.290",
      "text": "Okay, seeing none, this is a special meeting, and although I don't have any planned recognitions,"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": "00:14:10.290",
      "end": "00:14:15.640",
      "text": "I am going to give some leeway to the City Manager to introduce one of our new staff"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": "00:14:15.640",
      "end": "00:14:17.340",
      "text": "members."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": "00:14:17.340",
      "end": "00:14:21.100",
      "text": "Yes, Your Worship, thank you very much, and I'll take only a brief moment, but I wanted"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": "00:14:21.100",
      "end": "00:14:26.170",
      "text": "to seize on the opportunity to be able to introduce Council to Eliza Bennett."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": "00:14:26.170",
      "end": "00:14:31.360",
      "text": "Eliza is our new Director of Strategic Communications with the City of London, this very critical"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": "00:14:31.360",
      "end": "00:14:36.240",
      "text": "role for the City, so I felt it was important for Council to be able to put a face to a"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": "00:14:36.240",
      "end": "00:14:37.230",
      "text": "name."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": "00:14:37.230",
      "end": "00:14:43.510",
      "text": "Eliza is an extremely accomplished bilingual public sector executive with extensive experience"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": "00:14:43.510",
      "end": "00:14:52.450",
      "text": "in communications, strategic planning, and reputation management, as well as team leadership."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": "00:14:52.450",
      "end": "00:14:57.800",
      "text": "She has had many leadership roles in communications, including with the town of Tecumseh, the town"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": "00:14:57.800",
      "end": "00:15:03.080",
      "text": "of Aurora, the City of Laduk, and with the City of Greater Sudbury."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": "00:15:03.080",
      "end": "00:15:08.310",
      "text": "Eliza is not only being brave and taking on a new job with a new corporation, but also"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": "00:15:08.310",
      "end": "00:15:14.600",
      "text": "moving to a new city, and I know that you will join me in making sure that Eliza feels"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": "00:15:14.600",
      "end": "00:15:19.650",
      "text": "very welcome as she comes to do wonderful work with all of us for many years, we hope."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": "00:15:19.650",
      "end": "00:15:24.010",
      "text": "So welcome, Eliza, and I thank you for the opportunity to introduce her to you."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": "00:15:24.010",
      "end": "00:15:28.920",
      "text": "Yes, thank you very much, and welcome, I think because of today's special meeting, you'll"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": "00:15:28.920",
      "end": "00:15:32.770",
      "text": "have a completely false impression on the length of Council meetings."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": "00:15:32.770",
      "end": "00:15:34.920",
      "text": "But don't worry, you'll get used to it."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": "00:15:34.920",
      "end": "00:15:39.680",
      "text": "And again, welcome to the team, we're really happy to have you."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": "00:15:39.680",
      "end": "00:15:43.410",
      "text": "As this is a special meeting, we're not going to do any review of confidential matters"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": "00:15:43.410",
      "end": "00:15:46.870",
      "text": "considered in public session, there is no closed session, there's no confirmation of"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": "00:15:46.870",
      "end": "00:15:52.080",
      "text": "signing of previous minutes, no communications or petitions, no motions of which notice is"
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": "00:15:52.080",
      "end": "00:15:57.780",
      "text": "given, there is one report, the fifth report of a Special Community and Protective Services"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": "00:15:57.780",
      "end": "00:16:04.000",
      "text": "Committee meeting, I will turn it over to Chair Pelosa to present that report."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": "00:16:04.000",
      "end": "00:16:09.790",
      "text": "Thank you, Mr. Mayor, and we did have a special meeting of the Community Services Committee,"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": "00:16:09.790",
      "end": "00:16:13.370",
      "text": "and this was to deal with the timely funding transfer agreement that needed to come through"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": "00:16:13.370",
      "end": "00:16:18.660",
      "text": "before the end of the month, in which case this deals with the 911 transition funding"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": "00:16:18.660",
      "end": "00:16:22.840",
      "text": "support, where we go from the analog system to a new upgrade system for 911, which will"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": "00:16:22.840",
      "end": "00:16:29.810",
      "text": "allow residents and those in need to be able to transmit calls, videos and photos as well"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": "00:16:29.810",
      "end": "00:16:33.010",
      "text": "in real time to the 911 operators."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": "00:16:33.010",
      "end": "00:16:38.880",
      "text": "And this is allowing the city to accept the funding on behalf and enter a contract with"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": "00:16:38.880",
      "end": "00:16:44.590",
      "text": "the Solicitor General for $700,000 for the London Police Services and the London Fire"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": "00:16:44.590",
      "end": "00:16:47.230",
      "text": "Department to receive $900,000 in funding."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": "00:16:47.230",
      "end": "00:16:52.720",
      "text": "So I put this on the floor, realizing it was a unanimous vote at committee in a really"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": "00:16:52.720",
      "end": "00:16:54.320",
      "text": "short meeting on this one item."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": "00:16:54.320",
      "end": "00:16:56.060",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": "00:16:56.060",
      "end": "00:16:58.750",
      "text": "So the whole committee report is on the floor at any discussion."
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": "00:16:58.750",
      "end": "00:17:06.090",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": "00:17:06.090",
      "end": "00:17:13.950",
      "text": "Seeing none, I'm going to open that for voting."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": "00:17:13.950",
      "end": "00:17:21.200",
      "text": "Your worship, I'm going to vote, I have access to online voting."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": "00:17:21.200",
      "end": "00:17:22.130",
      "text": "It's a councilor."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": "00:17:22.130",
      "end": "00:17:26.000",
      "text": "Perfect."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": "00:17:26.000",
      "end": "00:17:38.970",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": "00:17:38.970",
      "end": "00:17:43.260",
      "text": "Yes, as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": "00:17:43.260",
      "end": "00:17:44.200",
      "text": "Councillor Hopkins and Ferreira."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": "00:17:44.200",
      "end": "00:17:50.130",
      "text": "I vote yay."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": "00:17:50.130",
      "end": "00:17:55.140",
      "text": "I vote yay as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": "00:17:55.140",
      "end": "00:17:56.100",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": "00:17:56.100",
      "end": "00:17:57.060",
      "text": "Close in the vote."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": "00:17:57.060",
      "end": "00:17:59.250",
      "text": "Motion carries 15 to 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": "00:17:59.250",
      "end": "00:18:00.540",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": "00:18:00.540",
      "end": "00:18:02.260",
      "text": "Thank you, Mr. Pelosa."
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": "00:18:02.260",
      "end": "00:18:03.240",
      "text": "We have no added reports."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": "00:18:03.240",
      "end": "00:18:08.810",
      "text": "No deferred matters, inquiries, I'm not going to allow any special meeting."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": "00:18:08.810",
      "end": "00:18:09.760",
      "text": "Emergent motions."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": "00:18:09.760",
      "end": "00:18:11.160",
      "text": "There are none."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": "00:18:11.160",
      "end": "00:18:14.460",
      "text": "We have three bylaws related to the decision we just made."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": "00:18:14.460",
      "end": "00:18:17.070",
      "text": "I'll look for a mover of all three."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": "00:18:17.070",
      "end": "00:18:23.150",
      "text": "That's bills 95, 96, and 97, altogether Councillor Frank, seconded by Councillor Hopkins."
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": "00:18:23.150",
      "end": "00:18:24.780",
      "text": "No debate on first reading."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": "00:18:24.780",
      "end": "00:18:30.200",
      "text": "So we'll open first reading for voting."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": "00:18:30.200",
      "end": "00:18:31.140",
      "text": "Councillor Neill."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": "00:18:31.140",
      "end": "00:18:37.220",
      "text": "I'm in votes."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": "00:18:37.220",
      "end": "00:18:39.150",
      "text": "Yes, as well."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": "00:18:39.150",
      "end": "00:18:42.740",
      "text": "Mr. Pelosa votes yes."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": "00:18:42.740",
      "end": "00:18:44.700",
      "text": "I vote yay."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": "00:18:44.700",
      "end": "00:18:47.830",
      "text": "Close in the vote, motion carries 15 to 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": "00:18:47.830",
      "end": "00:18:48.820",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": "00:18:48.820",
      "end": "00:18:50.320",
      "text": "I move in a seconder for second reading of those three bills."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": "00:18:50.320",
      "end": "00:18:54.140",
      "text": "I see Councillor Raman seconded by Councillor Stevenson."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": "00:18:54.140",
      "end": "00:19:00.730",
      "text": "Any discussion?"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": "00:19:00.730",
      "end": "00:19:01.680",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": "00:19:01.680",
      "end": "00:19:10.500",
      "text": "No discussion."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": "00:19:10.500",
      "end": "00:19:14.280",
      "text": "So we'll open that for voting."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": "00:19:14.280",
      "end": "00:19:18.590",
      "text": "Councillor Layton."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": "00:19:18.590",
      "end": "00:19:19.550",
      "text": "I vote yay."
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": "00:19:19.550",
      "end": "00:19:20.510",
      "text": "Close in the vote."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": "00:19:20.510",
      "end": "00:19:21.560",
      "text": "Motion carries 15 to 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": "00:19:21.560",
      "end": "00:19:22.530",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": "00:19:22.530",
      "end": "00:19:23.510",
      "text": "I move in a seconder for third reading of those bills."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": "00:19:23.510",
      "end": "00:19:25.770",
      "text": "Councillor Pelosa seconded by Councillor Ferreira."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": "00:19:25.770",
      "end": "00:19:35.930",
      "text": "With no debate on third reading, we'll open that for voting."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": "00:19:35.930",
      "end": "00:19:39.400",
      "text": "Councillor Layton votes yay."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": "00:19:39.400",
      "end": "00:19:42.010",
      "text": "I vote yay."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": "00:19:42.010",
      "end": "00:19:42.960",
      "text": "Close in the vote."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": "00:19:42.960",
      "end": "00:19:44.850",
      "text": "Motion carries 15 to 0."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": "00:19:44.850",
      "end": "00:19:46.450",
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": "00:19:46.450",
      "end": "00:19:48.880",
      "text": "To complete, all I need is a motion to adjourn."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": "00:19:48.880",
      "end": "00:19:51.230",
      "text": "Councillor Pelosa seconded by Councillor Ferreira."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": "00:19:51.230",
      "end": "00:19:54.460",
      "text": "All those in favor of adjournment?"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": "00:19:54.460",
      "end": "00:19:55.820",
      "text": "Motion carries."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": "00:19:55.820",
      "end": "00:20:00.670",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": "00:20:00.670",
      "end": "00:20:10.860",
      "text": "We're adjourned."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": "00:20:10.860",
      "end": "00:20:13.340",
      "text": "I'll just make one final reminder for those in the gallery."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": "00:20:13.340",
      "end": "00:20:18.460",
      "text": "The meeting that you're, I think you're planning on being here for is the SPPC meeting which"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": "00:20:18.460",
      "end": "00:20:19.460",
      "text": "starts at four."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": "00:20:19.460",
      "end": "00:20:22.900",
      "text": "That was a special council meeting for a one-on-one item agenda."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": "00:20:22.900",
      "end": "00:20:24.620",
      "text": "So that meeting will begin at four p.m."
    }
  ],
  "transcript_source": "lillian_skinner_archive",
  "transcript_source_url": "https://london.lillianskinner.ca/Meetings/Council/2023/03-28/.transcript.srt"
}